  "id": "slagwares",
  "note": "SLAG & WARES: a salvage pitch where the west road empties out onto the flats.\n\nThe tile's prose: a hand-cart the size of a room, roofed with corrugate and dug into the hardpan;\nsorted salvage on boards either side, in grades; a bell on a pole that rings whenever something\nheavy moves out on the flats; SLAG & WARES chalked on the tailboard.\n\nThe roof is the building. A low lapped vault of corrugate on six posts, eaves at a full storey,\nruns from the yard line back across the pit, so from Filament Yard you walk under it to the\ntailboard. The cart sits sunk to its axles in the spoil bank with its shafts down, the tailboard to\nthe road carrying the name in chalk. Trestles stand either side with the small grades at the\nfront, and the heavy grades are stacked at the back. The bell hangs off an arm on a pole at the\nfront corner, twice the height of the roof, where it can be heard on the flats.\n\nThe tile is one storey (`flags.floors: 1`), so the vault and the posts spend all of `h`.\n\nIt stands in for the `slagwares` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_board",
  "replaces": "slagwares",
